This folder is for Papers that were the foundation for the Concord.
Originaly written as stand alone hypothesis, these were combined into a stack which became the core of the Concord main book and other areas of the project.
(The Concord main book is a distilation of roughly 23 such papers of varying length)


"Unified paths of light" , now renamed for the second edition. Is a comparitive study of the world 8 largest religions in order to extract and distil the civilisation ethics kernal (Blaineys laws) 
that were used as the constitutional moral core of the Concord.
While the source material is theological, the resulting use of the derived ethics is not. 
The methodology of teh first edition was somewhat flawed and much data created during its writign was lost. the second edition is presented here in order to show full methodology and data.
The resultant Blaineys laws slightly differ from the first edition. It is not know if this is result of different set of 8 religions used, or an artifact of the better methodology. TBD.


Legacy tech continuity.md 
The issue of maintaining technology "legacy ladder" > developed into part of Knowledge Control system.

Worker Value.md
Issues of reltive renumeration for work > Developed into part of Ratchet system

Parallel Permutation Mathematics.md
Recursive evaluation of dogma in mathematics > Developed into Reality trees

The size 9 shoe problem.md
Why the greater good is the sum of all individual goods, not an average > developed into part of governance 

Paper 4 Blaineys Laws.md
The original version from the paper stack that was compiled into teh main Concord volume.


Closely related undeveloped material in the STUFF folder

Emergent Ethics and the Deep History of Blainey’s Laws.md
An interesting extension/offshot regarding Blainey laws and the possibility they are an emergenct ethical heuristic tool evolved by social pressures.
